From dc151726293079b129c1fd8d55993ad1cbda11d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Vis <118430440+mark-vis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 00:45:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 15/32] (b) v2, part b-3: first aid for \caption* with float

float.sty (frozen since 2001, loaded by many documents for [H] and by
algorithm.sty) replaces \caption by a definition that does not know the
star, so \caption*{Text} gave "Figure 2: *" with a list entry, followed
by "Text" (review finding N2: still old garbage with float).

The first aid (applied only to float.sty v1.3d, and only if the kernel
has the caption interface) keeps float's \caption for numbered captions
and lets \caption* use the kernel definition. For a type restyled by
float, \@caption is set for this one caption to float's caption code
\@float@c@<type>, which restores the previous \@caption and continues.
That code uses \fnum@<type> and \ext@<type> as the kernel did, and its
style macros put the label in a group ({\@fs@cfont #1:} #2, {\@fs@cfont
#1} #2), which \@caption@nolabel handles. So with the kernel's settings
for a replaced \@caption the caption has the style of float (ruled,
plain, boxed) without label, separator and list entry, and float's
optional argument after the caption still works.

Not covered: hyperref without \DocumentMetadata loaded after float
replaces \caption again (as for all floats; open question for
hyperref). The caption package replaces \caption anyway.

Documentation: ltfloat.dtx and usrguide mention the first aid; ltfloat
also names captcont (its own \caption*: numbered, no list entry) and
tufte-book among the packages that replace \caption.

Test: required/firstaid firstaid-float-caption (not restyled figure,
ruled table, numbered caption unchanged, optional argument of float).

The hook dumps of 15 lthooks and 2 lthooks2 tests list the new code for
package/float/after; their .tlg files are updated (additions only).
